![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The utility function `partitionRows` is not robust against non-array inputs. If `rows` is null, undefined, or not an array, accessing `rows.length` will throw a `TypeError`. To ensure the system fails closed gracefully, verify that `rows` is a valid array before checking its length.

```suggestion
function partitionRows(rows) {
  if (!Array.isArray(rows) || rows.length === 0) return [];
  const shardCount = Math.ceil(rows.length / TARGET_ROWS_PER_SHARD);
  const baseSize = Math.floor(rows.length / shardCount);
  const remainder = rows.length % shardCount;
  const partitions = [];
  let offset = 0;
  for (let index = 0; index < shardCount; index += 1) {
    const size = baseSize + (index < remainder ? 1 : 0);
    partitions.push(rows.slice(offset, offset + size));
    offset += size;
  }
  return partitions;
}
```

